  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed wraparound extension, by virtue of its excessive width and depth, detailed design, form, siting, bulk, fenestration, and proximity to the site boundary would appear visually intrusive, over dominant  and would harm the character and appearance of the host building and the surrounding Lakes Estate Conservation Area, which is not outweighed by any planning benefits, contrary with Sections 12 and 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024; Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021; Policy 44 of the DMD 2014; Policy 31 of the Core Strategy 2010, The Lakes Conservation Area Character Appraisal June 2015 and The Lakes Conservation Area Management Proposals June 2015."
